Dakkar
======

Dakkar is a file manager for Linux. It is a fork of Nemo, the Cinnamon file
manager by Linux Mint (https://github.com/linuxmint/nemo), which itself is
derived from GNOME Nautilus (GNOME Files,
https://gitlab.gnome.org/GNOME/nautilus).

License: GNU General Public License, version 2 or (at your option) any later
version (GPL-2.0-or-later), the same license as Nemo; see COPYING.
libnemo-extension keeps its LGPL license (COPYING.LIB, COPYING.EXTENSIONS),
and the documentation its own terms (COPYING-DOCS).

Dakkar is made by Kefkism (https://github.com/Kefkism).
Official repository and update channel: https://github.com/Kefkism/Dakkar

All copyright notices of Nemo, Nautilus and their contributors in the source
files are kept unchanged, as the GPL requires. Dakkar's own changes are
released under the same license.

See CREDITS for the projects Dakkar builds on and credits.
